{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 101, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the only learned op feeding node 1 with parameter-free pooling costs much more than replacing none/skip/pool there."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv on the direct input-output edge for a skip removes substantial capacity, as in experiment 3, whereas replacing a weak op costs little."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no edge creates a new learned path, giving a much larger gain than replacing an existing op, as in experiment 8."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv from the node1->output edge removes depth and capacity, while deleting skip or pool removes little."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is none, node 2's computation is dead, so adding a conv revives the deepest path and gives an outsized gain."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 1 is zero, so a conv on edge 1->2 processes nothing and its benefit largely vanishes."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 none, node 1 carries no signal, so adding a conv on edge 1->3 cannot help."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 2 does not reach the output, the direct edge carries more of the computation, so making it a conv matters more."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cutting a 3x3 conv on the final edge removes the deepest learned path, as in experiment 16, costing more than cutting a skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 2->3 is none, node 2 never reaches the output, so a conv added on edge 0->2 has almost no effect."}], "tok": 7778, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [4, "none"]], [["none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect"], [2, "nor_conv_